# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OSI — the single environment file for the whole project (root only).
# Committed on purpose: keep it SECRET-FREE. Put local secrets in .env.local
# (gitignored). Both compose files load this file via `env_file: - .env`.
#
# NODE_ENV and the host port are intentionally NOT set here:
#   - NODE_ENV is set per environment by the tooling / compose (dev vs prod).
#     Pinning it here breaks production builds (dev JSX runtime leaks in).
#   - The exposed host port default is 3010 everywhere (dev AND prod — same port);
#     override per run with `WEB_PORT=<port> docker compose ...` if needed.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Database (engine TBD — see src/database). Uncomment and fill in once chosen.
# Real credentials go in .env.local, never here.
# DB_PORT=5432
# POSTGRES_USER=osi
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
# POSTGRES_DB=osi
# DATABASE_URL=

# AI — the key is a SECRET: set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY in .env.local.
# The pre-search AI analysis was removed (2026-08-05): criteria are parsed
# synchronously at intake (zero tokens) and requests go straight to supplier
# search. Tokens are reserved for supplier research (E4).
AI_CHAT=false                           # true = per-request assistant chat (needs the API key)

# Test phase: shows the one-click demo-account login box on /login outside dev
# builds (dev always shows it). REMOVE/false before real users — the seeded
# demo credentials are public.
SHOW_TEST_LOGIN=true
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5      # gateway default; see src/server/ai/client.ts
# UPLOAD_DIR=/data/uploads              # attachment storage (compose mounts a named volume)
